{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790535266,"nonce":"75VIws+X7FfuKKTB5fU46fjsRBY=","message":"Decision: the build resolves isolate modules at compile time. There is no runtime fallback, and the embedded runtime is out of the picture.\n\n- The walker treats Isolate.spawn(\u003cstring literal\u003e, ...) as another root: it walks the named module and its imports as it walks the entry's, and the object compiles them all. This applies when Isolate is the isolate module's class, however it was imported. A spawned module is its own root and runs in its own instance, so it does not need to come before the module that spawns it.\n- A spawn whose module is not a literal cannot be resolved, so a wasm AOT build rejects it and names the call site. A module name that resolves to nothing is a build error too, as a missing import is.\n- The link keeps every spawned module's install and body reachable from wlift_isolate_run. A program that spawns nothing links as today.","files":null}]}